%%report safety-case-by-severity title: Safety Cases by severity entity: SafetyCase chart: pie x: severity y: records help: An airport safety occurrence or hazard investigation. How safety cases divide across severity, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(severity::text, '(unset)') AS severity, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_safety_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report safety-case-lifecycle title: Safety Case lifecycle entity: SafetyCase chart: bar x: state y: records help: An airport safety occurrence or hazard investigation. Where safety cases sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'logged' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'investigating', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'mitigated', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'resolved', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_safety_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report corrective-action-by-status title: Corrective Actions by status entity: CorrectiveAction chart: pie x: status y: records help: A remedial commitment belonging to one safety case, with an individual owner and verification evidence. How corrective actions divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_corrective_action WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report corrective-action-lifecycle title: Corrective Action lifecycle entity: CorrectiveAction chart: bar x: state y: records help: A remedial commitment belonging to one safety case, with an individual owner and verification evidence. Where corrective actions sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'proposed' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'accepted', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'implemented', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'validated', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_corrective_action WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report corrective-action-per-safety-case title: Corrective Actions per safety case entity: CorrectiveAction chart: bar x: safety_case y: records help: A remedial commitment belonging to one safety case, with an individual owner and verification evidence. Which safety case the most corrective actions belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.reference::text, '(none)') AS safety_case, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_corrective_action x LEFT JOIN bus_safety_case p ON p.id = x.safety_case_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report security-pass-by-status title: Security Passes by status entity: SecurityPass chart: pie x: status y: records help: A time-limited airside access authorisation for a named holder. How security passes divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_security_pass WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report security-pass-by-access-zone title: Security Passes by access zone entity: SecurityPass chart: pie x: access_zone y: records help: A time-limited airside access authorisation for a named holder. How security passes divide across access zone, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(access_zone::text, '(unset)') AS access_zone, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_security_pass WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report security-pass-lifecycle title: Security Pass lifecycle entity: SecurityPass chart: bar x: state y: records help: A time-limited airside access authorisation for a named holder. Where security passes sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'applied' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'issued', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'revoked', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'expired', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_security_pass WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report tariff-by-charge-type title: Tariffs by charge type entity: Tariff chart: pie x: charge_type y: records help: An approved unit price for an airport service, with a currency and effective interval. How tariffs divide across charge type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(charge_type::text, '(unset)') AS charge_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_tariff WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report tariff-by-unit title: Tariffs by unit entity: Tariff chart: pie x: unit y: records help: An approved unit price for an airport service, with a currency and effective interval. How tariffs divide across unit, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(unit::text, '(unset)') AS unit, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_tariff WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report tariff-top-currency title: Tariffs: the most common currency entity: Tariff chart: bar x: currency y: records help: An approved unit price for an airport service, with a currency and effective interval. The ten most frequent values of currency among tariffs; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(currency, '(blank)') AS currency, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_tariff WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report charge-by-status title: Charges by status entity: Charge chart: pie x: status y: records help: An assessed service charge against one movement. How charges divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_charge WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report charge-lifecycle title: Charge lifecycle entity: Charge chart: bar x: state y: records help: An assessed service charge against one movement. Where charges sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'assessed' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'approved', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'disputed', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'billed', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_charge WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report charge-top-currency title: Charges: the most common currency entity: Charge chart: bar x: currency y: records help: An assessed service charge against one movement. The ten most frequent values of currency among charges; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(currency, '(blank)') AS currency, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_charge WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report invoice-by-status title: Invoices by status entity: Invoice chart: pie x: status y: records help: An airport operator invoice to one airline in one currency. How invoices divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report invoice-lifecycle title: Invoice lifecycle entity: Invoice chart: bar x: state y: records help: An airport operator invoice to one airline in one currency. Where invoices sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'issued', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'void', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'settled', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report invoice-top-currency title: Invoices: the most common currency entity: Invoice chart: bar x: currency y: records help: An airport operator invoice to one airline in one currency. The ten most frequent values of currency among invoices; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(currency, '(blank)') AS currency, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report invoice-line-amount-per-month title: Average amount per month entity: InvoiceLine chart: line x: month y: average_amount help: A charge snapshot owned by one invoice. The average amount of invoice lines created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_amount FROM bus_invoice_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report invoice-line-per-invoice title: Invoice Lines per invoice entity: InvoiceLine chart: bar x: invoice y: records help: A charge snapshot owned by one invoice. Which invoice the most invoice lines belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.reference::text, '(none)') AS invoice, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_invoice_line x LEFT JOIN bus_invoice p ON p.id = x.invoice_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report invoice-line-amount-per-invoice title: Total amount per invoice entity: InvoiceLine chart: bar x: invoice y: total_amount help: A charge snapshot owned by one invoice. Invoice Lines added up on amount for each invoice, ten largest first. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.reference::text, '(none)') AS invoice, ROUND(SUM(x.amount)::numeric, 2) AS total_amount FROM bus_invoice_line x LEFT JOIN bus_invoice p ON p.id = x.invoice_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10
%%report receipt-by-status title: Receipts by status entity: Receipt chart: pie x: status y: records help: A payment received against an airline invoice and reconciled by finance. How receipts divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_receipt WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report receipt-by-method title: Receipts by method entity: Receipt chart: pie x: method y: records help: A payment received against an airline invoice and reconciled by finance. How receipts divide across method, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(method::text, '(unset)') AS method, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_receipt WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report receipt-lifecycle title: Receipt lifecycle entity: Receipt chart: bar x: state y: records help: A payment received against an airline invoice and reconciled by finance. Where receipts sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'recorded' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'reconciled', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'reversed', 2) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_receipt WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
